# rgbctl: give the logged-in desktop user (uaccess) access to the Corsair ONE a600 front light
# strips: lighting controller 1b1c:0d18, interface 2 (the one rgbctl uses).
# Independent of the corsair-one-a600 CoolerControl plugin, whose own rule only covers the
# cooling controller (0d27) and which removes that rule on uninstall.
# The interface number comes from ENV (set by systemd's 60-persistent-hidraw.rules): all ATTRS{}
# in one rule must match the same parent device, and bInterfaceNumber is on a different one.
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1b1c", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0d18", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="02", TAG+="uaccess"
